  /// in the rejected patches list is installed only if it is a dependency of
  /// another package. It is considered compliant with the patch baseline, and
  /// its status is reported as INSTALLED_OTHER . This is the default action
  /// if no option is specified. Windows Server : Windows Server doesn't
  /// support the concept of package dependencies. If a package in the
  /// rejected patches list and already installed on the node, its status is
  /// reported as INSTALLED_OTHER . Any package not already installed on the
  /// node is skipped. This is the default action if no option is specified.
  /// BLOCK All OSs : Packages in the rejected patches list, and packages that
  /// include them as dependencies, aren't installed by Patch Manager under
  /// any circumstances. State value assignment for patch compliance: If a
  /// package was installed before it was added to the rejected patches list,
  /// or is installed outside of Patch Manager afterward, it's considered
